| Technique | What it does | Trade-offs | Recommendation here |
|---|---|---|---|
| MLflow / ZenML / DVC registry | Full experiment tracking, artifacts, model lineage | Server/daemon + DB + client SDK; large dependency surface contradicting stdlib-lean setup | **Reject for now.** Revisit only if experiments multiply |
| File-based manifest in git (versions.json per task) | Version id, base model, training-data file hashes, metrics, status, timestamps, who promoted | No tooling; human-readable; diffable; scales fine to dozens of versions | **Adopt.** `ui_settings.json` already half-implements this; extend the version dicts (schema below) instead of adding a registry product |
| Directory-convention registry (`/data/loras/{task}/{version}/adapter/` + `meta.json`) | Adapter artifacts next to their metadata | Relies on naming discipline | Adopt alongside the manifest; manifest records the path + sha256 of the adapter dir |
| Semantic versioning / dated ids | `2026-10-02` today; collisions get ` %H:%M` appended | Dated ids sort naturally but encode nothing about compatibility | Keep dated ids (already established), add a monotonic `seq` integer for unambiguous ordering and rollback references |

## 5. Drift detection on prediction quality (when has the win model gone stale?)

| Technique | What it does | Trade-offs | Recommendation here |
|---|---|---|---|
| Page-Hinkley test | Cumulative deviation of a stream metric vs its running mean; alarms on sustained shift | ~20 lines, stdlib; tunable sensitivity (delta/gamma); designed for gradual drift | **First choice.** Run on the stream of win-model errors: `error = 1 - predicted_win_prob` for losses, `-predicted_win_prob` for wins |
| DDM (Drift Detection Method) | Binomial error-rate bounds (warning/drift at 2/3 std) | Simple; assumes binary error stream | Second choice; same data as P-H |
| ADWIN | Adaptive windowing, theoretical guarantees, no params | Real implementation is nontrivial; `river` library has it | Only if `river` is ever allowed as a dependency |
| Rolling calibration plot | Predicted win prob vs realized win rate by decile, last N tenders | No alarm logic, but humans read it instantly; also detects overconfidence | **Put in the generated report** - it doubles as the "should we switch models" evidence |
| Data drift on inputs (competitor count, price ratios) | Input distribution shift as leading indicator | Needs distribution comparisons (PSI/KS) | Cheap version: track min/median/max of bid-ratio per quarter in the report |

