## 9. Risks

- **Overfitting to few observations:** shrinkage priors and CIs must be shown, never hide n; a win-rate change after 3 tenders is noise.
- **Confounded elasticity:** we win easy jobs and lose hard ones; price-effect estimates from observational data are biased - state this in every report.
- **Feedback leakage into training data:** post-mortem text contains client names/competitor prices; LoRA data uploads must be reviewed for what should be learned vs merely recorded (privacy + Swiss procurement confidentiality).
- **Silent auto-promotion:** if the future automatic retraining pipeline calls `update` and anything auto-selects the new version, the gating above is void - `selected` must never be set by the training job.
- **Date-collision version ids** (`2026-10-10` vs `2026-10-10 14:33`) make rollback references fragile; the added `seq` fixes ordering but migration of existing ids is needed.
- **Golden-set rot:** curated eval examples stop representing reality; review them as part of the quarterly report cycle.
- **Report PII:** generated post-mortems quote competitor prices - access control on the reports folder before this leaves localhost.

